{"id":"n1-222","title":"～に耐える","romaji":"～ni taeru","jlptLevel":1,"shortExplanation":"To endure or withstand something; 'endure', 'withstand', 'tolerate'.","longExplanation":"The ～に耐える grammar point is used to express the concept of enduring or withstanding something, often involving a degree of difficulty or hardship. It can be translated as 'endure', 'withstand', or 'tolerate' in English. Here we focus on usage with nouns (e.g., a force or a hardship to endure).","formation":"Noun + に耐える","examples":[{"jp":"彼は厳しい修行に耐えた。","romaji":"Kare wa kibishii shugyou ni taeta.","en":"He endured the harsh training.","words":[{"surface":"彼","vocabId":"1483070","reading":"かれ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"厳しい","vocabId":"1262530","reading":"きびしい"},{"surface":"修行","vocabId":"2650010","reading":"しゅぎょう"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"耐え","vocabId":"1211310","reading":"たえる","baseForm":"耐える"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4,5]},{"jp":"この橋は強風に耐えられる。","romaji":"Kono hashi wa kyoufuu ni taerareru.","en":"This bridge can withstand strong winds.","words":[{"surface":"この","vocabId":null},{"surface":"橋","vocabId":"1237410","reading":"はし"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"強風","vocabId":"1236530","reading":"きょうふう"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"耐え","vocabId":"1211310","reading":"たえ","baseForm":"耐える"},{"surface":"られる","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4,5]},{"jp":"彼女は苦しみに耐えた。","romaji":"Kanojo wa kurushimi ni taeta.","en":"She endured the pain.","words":[{"surface":"彼女","vocabId":"1483150","reading":"かのじょ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"苦しみ","vocabId":"1244340","reading":"くるしみ"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"耐え","vocabId":"1211310","reading":"たえる","baseForm":"耐える"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[3,4]},{"jp":"この建物は地震に耐えることができます。","romaji":"Kono tatemono wa jishin ni taeru koto 